+config SUN50I_H713_ARISC
+	tristate "Allwinner H713 ARISC co-processor and HDMI front end"
+	depends on ARCH_SUNXI || COMPILE_TEST
+	depends on OF
+	help
+	  The H713 carries an OpenRISC core ("ARISC", "AR100") that owns the
+	  R_ peripherals, among them the HDMI hotplug pin, the EDID store and
+	  the DDC RAM. On a vendor system the secure monitor loads its
+	  firmware; mainline TF-A does not, so without this driver nothing
+	  runs on the core and the HDMI input stays dead.
+
+	  Say m here to load the firmware, complete the startup handshake it
+	  waits for, and export the HDMI services the receive driver needs.
+	  A module, not built in: the image comes out of /lib/firmware, which
+	  is not there yet when a built-in driver probes.
+
+	  If unsure, say N.
